4},{"segment":"turn_gap","start_seconds":131.424,"end_seconds":131.774},{"segment":"L3_12","start_seconds":131.774,"end_seconds":144.498},{"segment":"turn_gap","start_seconds":144.498,"end_seconds":144.848},{"segment":"L3_13","start_seconds":144.848,"end_seconds":148.517},{"segment":"turn_gap","start_seconds":148.517,"end_seconds":148.867},{"segment":"L3_14","start_seconds":148.867,"end_seconds":151.514},{"segment":"turn_gap","start_seconds":151.514,"end_seconds":151.864},{"segment":"response","start_seconds":151.864,"end_seconds":154.836},{"segment":"response_silence","start_seconds":154.836,"end_seconds":169.836},{"segment":"end","start_seconds":169.836,"end_seconds":172.298},{"segment":"tail","start_seconds":172.298,"end_seconds":172.598}],"human_review":"Owner listened and approved, 2026-10-09; exact-file audio scope.","encoded_verification":{"detected_pauses":[{"label":"reading_silence","detected_start":23.1511,"detected_end":53.3492,"detected_seconds":30.198},{"label":"response_silence","detected_start":154.669,"detected_end":169.862,"detected_seconds":15.193}],"decoded_peak_dbfs":-2.24,"decoded_clipped_samples":0,"decoded_seconds":172.598,"sha256_rechecked":true}},"installation_verified":"2026-10-09","teacher_content_review":"Required before assignment; no teacher confirmation recorded by installation."}'::jsonb, '8ad74eb6ab23d3d70b40cd5ce2caad4eb3052630d1c51ba4f2bdc74007ea41a2'),
('bh-ielts-targeted-listening-l4-v1', 'Agree the research plan: community food waste', 'guided_practice', 'extension-pack-02/df4c58e67b9778d30d7a77399a392e9a417670b36e8a557da73c560f6ec394d5/L4_practice_v1.mp3', 'df4c58e67b9778d30d7a77399a392e9a417670b36e8a557da73c560f6ec394d5', 'd4ad52b6-fd0f-4068-9982-28b89ff389c5', 'b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42', '0.1.0', 'listening', 'Complete all six answers. Write no more than TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer. Listen for the final confirmed details. You may pause or replay for practice. A quieter conversational passage in a library setting. Fully voiced speech, consistent intelligibility and matched playback level. No true whisper, background noise or answer masking.', 'Identify the final confirmed detail after a speaker changes an earlier suggestion.', '[{"id":"q1","prompt":"Agreed project topic","accepted_answers":["food waste"],"taxonomy_node_id":"d0aa0bad-ecfa-4598-8f2f-07e93d3fa59b","supporting_node_id":"f9064b63-e3f1-4bfa-8e8e-97a02756afb2"},{"id":"q2","prompt":"Method of collecting information","accepted_answers":["interviews"],"taxonomy_node_id":"d0aa0bad-ecfa-4598-8f2f-07e93d3fa59b","supporting_node_id":"f9064b63-e3f1-4bfa-8e8e-97a02756afb2"},{"id":"q3","prompt":"Participant group","accepted_answers":["shop owners"],"taxonomy_node_id":"d0aa0bad-ecfa-4598-8f2f-07e93d3fa59b","supporting_node_id":"f9064b63-e3f1-4bfa-8e8e-97a02756afb2"},{"id":"q4","prompt":"Minimum number of interviews","accepted_answers":["12","twelve"],"taxonomy_node_id":"d5b1fddb-ba6f-4be1-8513-bb26d822357a","supporting_node_id":"f9064b63-e3f1-4bfa-8e8e-97a02756afb2"},{"id":"q5","prompt":"Agreed meeting day","accepted_answers":["Thursday"],"taxonomy_node_id":"0dbe1c8f-403a-493f-afd3-c219310fb18a","supporting_node_id":"f9064b63-e3f1-4bfa-8e8e-97a02756afb2"},{"id":"q6","prompt":"Meeting place in the study centre","accepted_answers":["Room 4","Room Four","4","four"],"taxonomy_node_id":"d5b1fddb-ba6f-4be1-8513-bb26d822357a","supporting_node_id":"f9064b63-e3f1-4bfa-8e8e-97a02756afb2"}]'::jsonb, '{"scope":"Original IELTS-style guided Listening practice; not an official IELTS recording or a band assessment.","teacher_notes":"A quieter conversational passage in a library setting. Fully voiced speech, consistent intelligibility and matched playback level. No true whisper, background noise or answer masking.\n\nTranscript:\nMia: Let''s keep our voices down a little. This is the quiet study area. Did you look at the tutor''s comments on our project proposal?\nLeo: Yes. Our first idea, public transport, was too broad. I think food waste would be easier to investigate locally.\nMia: Agreed. Food waste it is. We can find out what happens to unsold food. Were you still thinking of using a questionnaire?\nLeo: I was, but the tutor wants us to explore people''s reasons, not just count responses. Let''s use interviews instead. We can ask follow-up questions when an answer isn''t clear.\nMia: That makes sense. At first I thought we could talk to customers, but they probably wouldn''t know how much gets thrown away.\nLeo: Exactly. Shop owners can explain that, so they should be our participants. We can ask how they plan their orders and deal with anything left over.\nMia: How many interviews do we need? I wrote fifteen in our first draft.\nLeo: The tutor said we must complete at least twelve. Fifteen would be useful, but twelve is the minimum we need to plan for.\nMia: Fine. Let''s divide the work evenly. Could we meet on Wednesday to check the interview questions before we contact anyone?\nLeo: I have a laboratory session then. Thursday works for me, and it still gives us enough time.\nMia: Thursday is good. Shall we meet back here in the library?\nLeo: We need to practise asking the questions aloud, so this quiet area won''t work. I''ve booked Room Four in the study centre. Let''s meet there.\nMia: Great. I''ll bring the draft questions. Before we leave, let''s check that none of them tells people what answer we expect.\nLeo: Good idea. We want to hear their experience, even if it doesn''t match what we predicted.\n\nKey and teaching notes:\nq1: food waste. Public transport was rejected as too broad; they agree on food waste. Primary: Explicit detail; supporting: Distractor resistance.\nq2: interviews. They replace the questionnaire with interviews to explore reasons. Primary: Explicit detail; supporting: Distractor resistance.\nq3: shop owners. Customers were considered, but shop owners know about unsold food. Primary: Explicit detail; supporting: Distractor resistance.\nq4: 12 / twelve. Fifteen would be useful; the tutor requires at least twelve. Primary: Numerical information; supporting: Distractor resistance.\nq5: Thursday. Wednesday conflicts with Leo''s laboratory session; Thursday is agreed. Primary: Dates and times; supporting: Distractor resistance.\nq6: Room 4 / Room Four / 4 / four. The library is unsuitable for speaking practice; Leo has booked Room Four. Primary: Numerical information; supporting: Distractor resistance."}'::jsonb, true, '{"audio_approval":{"reviewer":"Sobbi (Brains Heist owner)","date":"2026-10-09","source_statement":"Listened and approved","scope":"Approval of the two delivered practice recordings. Teacher confirmation of editorial quality, keys, mappings, difficulty/timing and originality remains required for assignment. No calibration, device, capacity or wider-release approval inferred.","files":[{"file":"L3_practice_v1.mp3","sha256":"051a7be84978ff4b530dfb1dbf47f2b2945b73e64204366bd4d39d1d7e090d4e"},{"file":"L4_practice_v1.mp3","sha256":"df4c58e67b9778d30d7a77399a392e9a417670b36e8a557da73c560f6ec394d5"}]},"draft_reference":"docs/ielts/practice/LISTENING_EXTENSION_02_DRAFT.json","draft_content_sha256":"cd0838ce0f7363b6e39a0f7ad4e685643afc03d9f84e85c2e5332942604322b8","script_sha256":"f174fe414577e637917cff434edab1d08a18b8dbc32cd316dabe59d7e3c5b532","voices":{"Mia":"Katie","Leo":"James"},"provider":"ElevenLabs","model":"eleven_multilingual_v2